+package xz_test
+
+// Hegel property tests for github.com/ulikunitz/xz.
+//
+// Oracles: XZ Utils' `xz` command-line tool (5.4.x on this machine; a stream
+// written by the Go Writer must decode with `xz -dc`, `xz --robot -l` must see
+// the blocks and the check the Writer was configured for, and a stream written
+// by `xz` with any option set must decode with the Go Reader - for the .xz
+// container, the classic .lzma format (`--format=lzma`) and raw LZMA2 chunk
+// sequences (`--format=raw --lzma2`)), plus the round trip Writer->Reader under
+// random configurations and read/write chunkings, the documented Verify rules
+// for the configuration structs, and the io.Reader/io.WriteCloser contracts.
+//
+// Every property draws one case record built from generator values. The bulk
+// bytes of a case are a dataSpec (a size, a kind and a PRNG seed, rendered by
+// fill, so that a 256 KB input is three draws), a writer's chunking a
+// writePlan (sizes taken modulo what is left, the empty plan one Write), a
+// reader's chunking a readPlan (buffer sizes cycled, some empty), the writer
+// configurations records rendered into the library's config structs by pure
+// methods, the xz tool's options a record rendered to its argument list, and a
+// corruption a mutation record applied at a position taken modulo the stream's
+// length. The shapes of the recorded bugs (bugs.toml) are drawn by default and
+// the properties that meet them fail, naming the shape (STYLE.md rule 11); the
+// pins in hegel_pins_test.go are the regression examples and
+// hegel_shapes_test.go has one property per bug over its shape region alone.
+// HEGEL_NO_KNOWN=1 switches the known shapes off (noKnown, Known below) for a
+// run that looks past the bugs.
+//
+// Set XZ_COLLECT=1 to make the properties record mismatches instead of failing
+// and print them (shortest first) at the end of each test.
+
+import (
+	"bytes"
